>long-range stethescope, also allowing a certain chance to identify items.

It sounds like when you (a)pply it, you get something kinda like
the wand of probing.  Unlike the wand and stethoscope, you don't get
only the Level, AC, HP, and alignment.  You also get speed, magic resistance,
description of attacks, and what you get from eating its corpse
(if it even leaves one).

Invoking it would be just like a blessed scroll of identify, and then some.
Not only do you find out that the thonged club is an aklys, but you
also know what damage it does, as well as every other weapon you
choose to identify.  Identifying gems gives you value as well as name.

Unfortunately, like many AD&D artifacts, there is a minor downside
to invoking the artifact.  When you invoke it, not only do you get
your identify, but you also get the effect of a scroll of amnesia.
After all the more you read from the Netnews and the spoilers,
the more you kick yourself for forgetting stupid things when you die.

I can only imagine how many elves and gnomes, etc. will try to
steal this artifact from you.  Or maybe all the soldiers in the
barracks are waiting for this tool, so that they can find the
amulet and ascend before you stop them!

